    qs.push({n:27,title:'Human bias in AI decisions',stimulus:`STIMULUS TRANSCRIPT (original text; not a reproduction of the unavailable 2025 exam video):\nA model trained on photographs of professional uniforms repeatedly identifies a medical worker as a nurse when the subject is female and as a doctor when male. In a separate experiment, unfamiliar types of footwear are not recognised because the training set contains only a narrow range of shoes.`,parts:[{id:'a',...written('Explain how human bias affects the usefulness of AI solutions. Support your answer with explicit references to BOTH examples in the stimulus.',6,200,'An AI model derives patterns from the examples selected and labelled by people. If the dataset over-represents traditional gender roles, the uniform classifier may learn a misleading association between being male and being a doctor. This produces incorrect outputs for female doctors and compromises trust. Likewise, a footwear classifier trained on only familiar shoe styles may fail to recognise uncommon designs, reducing its usefulness for diverse users. Bias can enter through data selection, labels and the assumptions of developers. Representative datasets, bias audits and human review can reduce these errors, although they require ongoing monitoring after deployment.',[criterion('Explains how human assumptions influence selection or labels','human|develop|bias|assum|label|select|collect'),criterion('Links bias in training data to learned patterns','train|dataset|data','pattern|learn|model|output'),criterion('Explicitly explains the gender/profession example','doctor|nurse|medical|gender|female|male'),criterion('Explicitly explains the footwear example','shoe|footwear|design|style'),criterion('Explains impact on accuracy, fairness or fitness for purpose','inaccur|error|unfair|discriminat|trust|useful|reliab|misclassif'),criterion('Offers a concrete mitigation or recognises amplification','divers|represent|audit|test|review|monitor|mitigat|amplif|oversight')])}]});
    const marks=qs.reduce((s,q)=>s+q.parts.reduce((a,p)=>a+p.marks,0),0);
